    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneI_13.2/p@20293",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "GLOUCESTER.\nO Nell, sweet Nell, if thou dost love thy lord,\nBanish the canker of ambitious thoughts.\nAnd may that hour when I imagine ill\nAgainst my King and nephew, virtuous Henry,\nBe my last breathing in this mortal world!\nMy troublous dreams this night doth make me sad.",
